2)\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary standard for service choreography, entrances, litanies, and hierarchy.\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Specific rubrics for the Daily Cycle (Pt. II), Menaion (Pt. III), Triodion (Pt. IV), and Pentecostarion (Pt. V).\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Card-by-Card Maximalist Checkpoints\n\n### Card 1: General Info Card\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I & II (Headers of all 20 Paradigms); Ordo Celebrationis §§ 1–24.*\n\n- [ ] **Date Grounding**: Formats Civil Date, Julian/Old Calendar Date, and Day of the Week.\n- [ ] **Full Commemoration Title**: Unabbreviated official name and title of the commemorated feast/saint.\n- [ ] **Dolnytsky Rank & Symbol**: Canonical Rank (1 to 7) and liturgical classification (Simple, 6 Stichera, Doxology, Polyeleos, Vigil, Great Feast).\n- [ ] **Tone & Eothinon Cycle**: Octoechos Tone of the Week (1–8) and Matins Resurrection Gospel Eothinon number (1–11 on Sundays).\n- [ ] **Liturgical Season**: Exact liturgical period (Octoechos, Triodion, Pentecostarion, Dormition/Nativity Fast).\n- [ ] **Combination Formula**: Full Dolnytsky Part II heading formula (e.g., *\"Dolnytsky Part II, Case 2: Simple Weekday service combined with Saint without Polyeleos\"*).\n- [ ] **Vestment Color & Citation**: Appointed liturgical color, alternative permitted colors, and *Ordo Celebrationis* § citation.\n- [ ] **Fasting Degree**: Explicit rule (Strict Fast / Xerophagy, Wine & Oil, Fish, Fast-free, or No fasting restriction).\n- [ ] **Prostrations & Kneeling Rule**: Explicit statement of whether prostrations/kneeling are permitted or forbidden (e.g., forbidden on Sundays per Canon 20 of Nicaea I) and Great Lenten metania counts.\n\n---\n\n### Card 2: Daily / Great Vespers Card\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 1–100), Part II, Ch. 1; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 25–45.*\n\n- [ ] **Opening & Psalm 103**: Priest's opening exclamation, Opening Prayers, and Psalm 103 (with priest's silent Lucernarium prayers before the Holy Doors).\n- [ ] **Great Litany & Kathisma**: Great Litany; Kathisma determination (Kathisma 1 on Saturday evening; Kathisma 18 on weekdays; Kathisma omitted if preceding day had a Vigil per Dolnytsky Pt. I).\n- [ ] **\"Lord, I Call\" (Stichoi & Stichera Counts)**:\n  - Exact Psalm verses (Ps 140, 141, 129, 116).\n  - Exact distribution ratio (e.g. Weekday = 6: 3 Octoechos in Tone of the Week + 3 Menaion in Tone of the Saint; Sunday = 10: 7/4 Octoechos + 3/3 Menaion).\n  - Glory (Doxastikon): Menaion Saint Doxastikon (or combined).\n  - Both now (Theotokion): Sunday Tone Dogmatikon on Saturday evening; Dismissal Theotokion from Horologion in the tone of the Doxastikon and day of the week on weekdays.\n- [ ] **Entrance & O Gladsome Light**: Entrance with Censer (Vigil/Polyeleos/Sunday) vs. No Entrance (Holy Doors closed on ordinary weekdays); *Phos Hilaron* chanted or read.\n- [ ] **Prokeimenon & Old Testament Readings**: Appointed Great Prokeimenon vs. Daily Prokeimenon (Tone and verses); Paremias with deacon cues (*\"Wisdom!\"*).\n- [ ] **Litanies**: Fervent Litany, *Vouchsafe, O Lord* (read), and Litany of Supplication.\n- [ ] **Litiya & Artoklasia (if Vigil)**: Narthex procession, Litiya stichera, Litiya litany, and Artoklasia bread/wheat/wine/oil blessing.\n- [ ] **Aposticha**: 3 Aposticha stichera with appointed psalm verses; Glory; Both now (Theotokion/Stavrotheotokion matching tone).\n- [ ] **Nunc Dimittis & Dismissal Troparia Chain**: *Song of Simeon*, Trisagion to Our Father, and the exact chain of Troparia (handling 1 vs. 2 Saints) + Dismissal Theotokion.\n\n---\n\n### Card 3: Small / Great Compline Card\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 100–150), Part II, Ch. 3; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 76–85.*\n\n- [ ] **Opening & Fixed Psalms**: Blessing, Trisagion, Psalms 4, 6, 12, 24, 30, 90 (or Great Compline 3-section psalmody with *\"God is with us\"*).\n- [ ] **Canon**: Canon of the Theotokos from the Octoechos (Odes 1–9 with Heirmoi and refrains).\n- [ ] **Troparia Sequence**: Weekday Troparion, Temple Troparion, Saint Troparion, *\"O God of our fathers...\"*, *\"Reckon all our enemies...\"*, Daily Theotokion.\n- [ ] **Concluding Prayers**: Prayer of St. Ephrem (with 4 great prostrations and 12 metanias if Lent), Prayer of St. Basil, Prayer of Paul the Monk (*\"O Spotless, undefiled...\"*), Prayer of Antiochus (*\"And grant to us, Master, as we depart to sleep...\"*), Mutual Forgiveness ceremony, and final litany.\n\n---\n\n### Card 4: Midnight Office Card\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 150–180), Part II, Ch. 3; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 76–85.*\n\n- [ ] **Daily Variant**: Psalm 50, Kathisma 17 (Psalm 118 in 3 stases), Creed, Midnight Troparia (*\"Behold, the Bridegroom comes...\"*), Prayer of the Hours, Prayer of St. Mardarius (*\"O God and Master, Lord the Father Almighty...\"*), and mutual forgiveness.\n- [ ] **Saturday Variant**: Psalm 50, Kathisma 9, Saturday Troparia (*\"Uncreated Nature...\"*).\n- [ ] **Sunday Variant**: Canon to the Holy and Undivided Trinity (in the Tone of the Octoechos), Sessional Hymns, and Hymns to the Trinity (*\"It is truly right to glorify the Trinity...\"*).\n\n---\n\n### Card 5: Daily / Great Matins Card (12 Gates)\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 180–220), Part II, Ch. 2; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 46–75.*\n\n- [ ] **Gate 1 — Royal Office & Hexapsalmos**: Royal Psalms (19 & 20), Royal Troparia, Six Psalms (Ps 3, 37, 62, 87, 102, 142) with the priest reciting the 12 Morning Prayers silently before the Holy Doors.\n- [ ] **Gate 2 — \"God is the Lord\" / \"Alleluia\"**: 4 verses with refrains; Troparia sequence (Resurrectional x2 / Feast x3 / Saint x2 / Glory... Saint / Both now... Dismissal Theotokion).\n- [ ] **Gate 3 — Kathismata & Sessional Hymns**: Appointed Kathismata with Small Litanies; Sessional Hymns with Theotokia (Tone and source).\n- [ ] **Gate 4 — Polyeleos, Megalynarion & Evlogitaria**: Polyeleos Psalms (134 & 135), Festal Megalynarion, Resurrectional Evlogitaria (*\"Blessed art Thou, O Lord, teach me Thy statutes\"*).\n- [ ] **Gate 5 — Hypakoe, Anavathmoi & Prokeimenon**: Hypakoe of the Tone, Gradual Hymns (Anavathmoi), Matins Prokeimenon of the Tone/Feast with verse.\n- [ ] **Gate 6 — Matins Gospel & Eothinon Linkage**: Priest Gospel reading (*\"Wisdom! Stand upright! Let us hear the Holy Gospel\"*), Eothinon Resurrection Gospel #1–11 (on Sunday) or Festal Gospel, *\"Having beheld the Resurrection of Christ\"*, Psalm 50 with Post-Gospel Stichera.\n- [ ] **Gate 7 — The Canon Structure**:\n  - Odes 1–8: Exact composition of every canon (Resurrection + Cross-Resurrection + Theotokos + Saint), total count (14, 12, 8, 6), Heirmoi, Katavasia (seasonal Katavasia at Odes 3, 6, 8, 9).\n  - After Ode 3: Sessional Hymns and Kontakion of the Saint.\n  - After Ode 6: Kontakion and Ikos of the Feast/Resurrection/Saint, Synaxarion reading.\n- [ ] **Gate 8 — Ode 9 Magnificat**: Magnificat (*\"My soul magnifies the Lord\"* with *\"More honorable than the Cherubim\"*) OR Festal Refrains and Heirmos of Ode 9.\n- [ ] **Gate 9 — Exapostilarion & Praises**: Eothinon Exapostilarion / Saint Exapostilarion / Theotokion; Praises Psalms (Ps 148, 149, 150) with 8, 6, or 4 Stichera; Glory / Both now.\n- [ ] **Gate 10 — Doxology**: Great Doxology (chanted with concluding Trisagion) on Sundays/Feasts OR Small Doxology (read) on simple weekdays.\n- [ ] **Gate 11 — Dismissal Troparion**: Sunday Odd/Even Tone Troparion or Saint Troparion.\n- [ ] **Gate 12 — Litanies & Conclusion**: Litany of Supplication, Fervent Litany, and Final Dismissal.\n\n---\n\n### Card 6: The Hours Card (1st, 3rd, 6th, 9th Hours)\n*Source: Dolnytsky Typikon Part I (pp. 209–220), Part II, Ch. 4; Ordo Celebrationis §§ 86–99.*\n\n- [ ] **Fixed 3-Psalm Sequences**: 1st Hour (Ps 5, 89, 100), 3rd Hour (Ps 16, 24, 50), 6th Hour (Ps 53, 54, 90), 9th Hour (Ps 83, 84, 85).\n- [ ] **Troparia & Kontakia Rotation**: Exact cycling rules between Sunday, Feast, Patron, and Saint across the four hours.\n- [ ] **Verses & Prayers of the Hours**: Appointed verses (*Order my steps*, *Blessed is the Lord*, *Let Thy compassions quickly overtake us*, *Forsake us not to the end*); Prayer of the Hours (*\"You Who at all times...\"*), Prayer of St. Mardarius, Prayer of St. Basil, and Prayer of St. Ephrem (in Lent).\n\n---\n\n### Card 7: Divine Liturgy Card\n*Source: Ordo Celebrationis §§ 35–45; Dolnytsky Typikon Appendix.*\n\n- [ ] **Antiphons**: 1st, 2nd, and 3rd Antiphons (Daily Psalm verses vs. Typika Psalms 102 & 145 + Beatitudes vs. Festal Antiphons) with proper Refrains.\n- [ ] **Little Entrance & Introit**: Entrance with the Gospel Book; Introit verse (*\"Come, let us worship and fall down before Christ...\"* with appointed feast refrain).\n- [ ] **Troparia & Kontakia Chain**: Exact insertion sequence (Temple, Feast, Sunday, Patron, Saint, Kontakion of the Feast / *\"Steadfast Protectress of Christians\"*).\n- [ ] **Trisagion Hymn**: Trisagion (*\"Holy God...\"*) vs. Baptismal Hymn (*\"As many as have been baptized into Christ...\"*) vs. Cross Hymn (*\"Before Thy Cross we bow down...\"*).\n- [ ] **Readings & Precedence**:\n  - Prokeimenon (Tone, verses, single vs. double reading precedence).\n  - Epistle (Pericope, composite Sunday + Saint rules).\n  - Alleluia (Tone, 2 appointed verses).\n  - Gospel (Pericope, Lucan/Matthean/Johannine sequence).\n- [ ] **Eucharistic Canon & Kinonikon**: Hymn to the Mother of God (*\"It is truly right...\"* vs. Festal Irmos/Zadostoinik), Kinonikon (Communion Verse) precedence (Sunday *\"Praise the Lord from the heavens\"* + Saint *\"In everlasting remembrance shall the righteous be\"*).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Double-Blind TDD Verification Rule\nEvery audited card must be validated by dedicated parameterized tests in `tests/test_canonical_audit_truth.py` asserting exact field compliance against this standard. A card cannot be marked `PASS` in any session report without an accompanying green test assertion.\n","Description":"Codify Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard in .agents/references/","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"c:\\Users\\augus\\OneDrive\\Documents\\Google Antigravity\\Projects\\Typikon Coded\\.agents\\references\\canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md","toolAction":"Writing canonical maximalist digest standard","toolSummary":"Writing canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md"}}]}
