{"step_index":692,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:16:07Z","content":"I will update `.agents/references/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md` in the artifact directory and copy it to the references library, expanding it to cover all 20 canonical non-Triodion cases and all N Triodion/Pentecostarion seasonal cases with a uniform data presentation.","thinking":"**Considering Uniform Applicability**\n\nI'm now contemplating whether the standard can be enhanced to apply universally across all twenty cases outside the triodia and the specific 'n' case within it. The key is ensuring a consistent data presentation, regardless of the card or day. This unified approach seems promising, offering clarity.\n\n\n**Expanding Uniformity's Scope**\n\nI'm expanding the scope, aiming for uniformity across all twenty cases, excluding the Triodia and the 'n' sub-case. My focus remains on ensuring a consistent data representation across the entire corpus. This approach seems logical, enhancing clarity.\n\n\n\n**Analyzing Case Diversity**\n\nNow, I'm analyzing how these diverse scenarios, especially cases 17 through 20, fit into the broader framework. I'm focusing on the afterfeast, the weekdays, Saturdays, and Sundays in both Lenten and Bright weeks as they relate to all 'n' cases within the Triodia. The core concept is seamless integration and a consistent format for each scenario to minimize any possible confusion.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Enhanced Universal Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard covering all 20 Paradigms and all Triodia cases with uniform data presentation.","UserFacing":true},"CodeContent":"# Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard (Universal Edition)\n\n> **Authority**: 2010 Lviv Typikon; Dolnytsky Typikon Parts I–V (1899); Ordo Celebrationis (1944/1996).  \n> **Scope**: Uniformly applicable to all 20 Non-Triodion Paradigms and all N Triodia Cases (Lenten Triodion & Pentecostarion).  \n> **Goal**: 100% consistent data presentation across every card of any day, where every card deterministically evaluates to `PASS`.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Hierarchy of Canonical Authority (Rule 2)\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary standard for service choreography, entrances, litanies, and hierarchy.\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Specific rubrics for Daily Cycle (Pt. II), Menaion (Pt. III), Triodion (Pt. IV), and Pentecostarion (Pt. V).\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Universal Data Presentation Schema for Every Card\n\nEvery service card generated in the **Service Rubrics Digest** MUST render in this exact 6-tier uniform structure:\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│ [TIER 1] CARD HEADER & BADGES                                               │\n│ • Service Title (e.g. \"DAILY VESPERS\", \"GREAT MATINS (ALL-NIGHT VIGIL)\")    │\n│ • Appointed Vestment Color Badge & Fasting Rule Badge (if service-specific) │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [TIER 2] OPENING & ENTRANCE CHOREOGRAPHY                                    │\n│ • Opening Blessing & Psalmody (Psalm 103, Hexapsalmos, or Royal Office)     │\n│ • Sanctuary / Door State & Entrance Type (No Entrance, Censer, Gospel Book)  │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [TIER 3] PSALMODY & KATHISMA DETERMINATION                                  │\n│ • Appointed Kathismata numbers & Sessional Hymns (with Tone and Theotokion) │\n│ • Kathisma Omission rules (e.g. post-Vigil omission, Lenten 3-Kathisma rule)│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [TIER 4] CORE HYMN STACK & PROPORTIONAL RATIOS                              │\n│ • Exact Hymn counts and distribution (Octoechos vs. Menaion vs. Triodion)   │\n│ • Doxastikon (Glory) & Theotokion / Dogmatikon (Both now) with Tone Matching│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [TIER 5] SCRIPTURE READINGS & LITANIES                                      │\n│ • Prokeimena (Tone, verses, refrains) & Paremias / Epistle / Gospel pericopes│\n│ • Litanies sequence (Great, Small, Fervent, Supplication, Special petitions)│\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│ [TIER 6] DISMISSAL & CONCLUDING APODOSIS                                    │\n│ • Dismissal Troparia chain (Resurrection -> Feast -> Patron -> Saint)       │\n│ • Dismissal Theotokion in the appointed tone                                │\n│ • Priest's Final Benediction naming all commemorated saints                 │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. The 20 Canonical Paradigms (Non-Triodion Season)\n\nThe standard enforces exact hymn distributions across all 20 canonical cases from Dolnytsky Part II:\n\n| Case ID | Liturgical Condition | Vespers Stichera (Lord I Call) | Matins Canons (Odes 1–8) | Matins Praises (Ainoi) | Liturgy Troparia / Kontakia |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **CASE_01** | Sunday + 1 Simple Saint | 10 (7 Octoechos + 3 Saint) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Cross-Res + 2 Theotokos + 6 Saint) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Sunday Stichera) | Sunday Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Glory/Both now: Sunday Kontakion |\n| **CASE_02** | Weekday + 1 Simple Saint | 6 (3 Octoechos + 3 Saint) | 14 (4 Oct 1 + 4 Oct 2 + 6 Saint) | Small Doxology (No Praises Stichera) | Saint Troparion ➔ Glory/Both now: Dismissal Theotokion |\n| **CASE_03** | Sunday + 2 Saints | 10 (4 Octoechos + 3 Saint A + 3 Saint B) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Theotokos + 4 Saint A + 4 Saint B) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Sunday Stichera) | Sunday Troparion ➔ Saint A ➔ Saint B ➔ Sunday Kontakion |\n| **CASE_04** | Weekday + 2 Saints | 6 (3 Saint A + 3 Saint B) | 14 (4 Oct 1 + 2 Oct 2 + 4 Saint A + 4 Saint B) | Small Doxology (No Praises Stichera) | Saint A ➔ Saint B ➔ Glory: Kontakion Saint B ➔ Both now: Saint A |\n| **CASE_05** | Sunday + Saint on 6 (Doxology) | 10 (4 Octoechos + 6 Saint) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Theotokos + 8 Saint) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Saint) [Great Doxology] | Sunday Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Glory: Kontakion Saint ➔ Both now: Sunday |\n| **CASE_06** | Weekday + Saint on 6 (Doxology) | 6 (All 6 Saint) | 14 (6 Octoechos + 8 Saint) | 4 (All 4 Saint) [Great Doxology] | Saint Troparion ➔ Glory: Kontakion Saint ➔ Both now: Theotokion |\n| **CASE_07** | Sunday + Polyeleos Saint | 10 (4 Octoechos + 6 Saint; Glory: Saint; Both: Dogmatikon) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Theotokos + 8 Saint; Katavasia: Season) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Saint; Glory: Saint; Both: Blessed art Thou) | Sunday Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Sunday Kontakion ➔ Glory: Saint ➔ Both: Steadfast Protectress |\n| **CASE_08** | Weekday + Polyeleos Saint | 8 (All 8 Saint; Glory: Saint; Both: Theotokion) | 12 (4 Theotokos + 8 Saint; Katavasia: Season) | 4 (All 4 Saint; Glory: Saint; Both: Theotokion) [Great Doxology] | Saint Troparion ➔ Glory: Saint Kontakion ➔ Both now: Steadfast Protectress |\n| **CASE_09** | Sunday + Vigil Saint | 10 (3 Octoechos + 3 Litiya + 4 Saint; Litiya & Artoklasia) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Theotokos + 8 Saint; Katavasia: Season) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Saint; Glory: Saint; Both: Blessed art Thou) | Sunday Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Sunday Kontakion ➔ Glory: Saint ➔ Both: Steadfast Protectress |\n| **CASE_10** | Weekday + Vigil Saint | 8 (All 8 Saint; Litiya & Artoklasia) | 12 (4 Theotokos + 8 Saint; Katavasia: Season) | 4 (All 4 Saint) [Great Doxology] | Saint Troparion ➔ Glory: Saint Kontakion ➔ Both now: Steadfast Protectress |\n| **CASE_11** | Great Feast of the Lord on Sunday | 10 (All 10 Feast; Octoechos suppressed) | 14 (All 14 Feast; Octoechos suppressed; Festal Katavasia) | 8 (All 8 Feast; Octoechos suppressed) | Festal Troparion x3 ➔ Glory/Both now: Festal Kontakion |\n| **CASE_12** | Great Feast of the Lord on Weekday | 10 (All 10 Feast; Litiya & Artoklasia) | 14 (All 14 Feast; Festal Katavasia) | 8 (All 8 Feast) [Great Doxology] | Festal Troparion x3 ➔ Glory/Both now: Festal Kontakion |\n| **CASE_13** | Great Feast of Theotokos on Sunday | 10 (4 Octoechos + 6 Feast; Glory: Feast; Both: Dogmatikon) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Theotokos + 8 Feast; Festal Katavasia) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Feast; Glory: Feast; Both: Blessed art Thou) | Sunday Troparion ➔ Feast Troparion ➔ Sunday Kontakion ➔ Feast Kontakion |\n| **CASE_14** | Great Feast of Theotokos on Weekday | 8 (All 8 Feast; Litiya & Artoklasia) | 12 (All 12 Feast; Festal Katavasia) | 4 (All 4 Feast) [Great Doxology] | Feast Troparion x3 ➔ Glory/Both now: Feast Kontakion |\n| **CASE_15** | Forefeast / Afterfeast on Sunday | 10 (4 Octoechos + 3 Feast + 3 Saint) | 14 (4 Res + 2 Theotokos + 4 Feast + 4 Saint) | 8 (4 Octoechos + 4 Feast) | Sunday Troparion ➔ Feast Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Sunday Kontakion ➔ Feast Kontakion |\n| **CASE_16** | Forefeast / Afterfeast on Weekday | 6 (3 Feast + 3 Saint) | 12 (6 Feast + 6 Saint; Katavasia: Feast) | Small Doxology (or 4 Feast on Doxology day) | Feast Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Glory: Saint ➔ Both now: Feast Kontakion |\n| **CASE_17** | Saturday + Simple Saint | 6 (3 Octoechos + 3 Saint; Glory: Saint; Both: Dogmatikon of Tone) | 14 (4 Oct Mart + 4 Oct Comp + 6 Saint) | Small Doxology (No Praises Stichera) | Troparion of Saturday ➔ Saint ➔ Glory/Both: Martyria Theotokion |\n| **CASE_18** | Saturday + Saint on 6 (Doxology) | 6 (All 6 Saint; Both: Dogmatikon of Tone) | 14 (6 Octoechos + 8 Saint) | 4 (All 4 Saint) [Great Doxology] | Saint Troparion ➔ Glory: Saint Kontakion ➔ Both: Theotokion |\n| **CASE_19** | Saturday + Polyeleos / Vigil Saint | 8 (All 8 Saint; Litiya & Artoklasia) | 12 (4 Theotokos + 8 Saint; Katavasia: Season) | 4 (All 4 Saint) [Great Doxology] | Saint Troparion ➔ Glory: Saint Kontakion ➔ Both: Steadfast Protectress |\n| **CASE_20** | Saturday + Forefeast / Afterfeast | 6 (3 Feast + 3 Saint; Both: Dogmatikon of Tone) | 12 (6 Feast + 6 Saint; Katavasia: Feast) | Small Doxology (or 4 Feast if Doxology) | Feast Troparion ➔ Saint ➔ Glory: Saint ➔ Both now: Feast Kontakion |\n\n---\n\n## 4. The N Triodia Cases (Lenten Triodion & Pentecostarion)\n\nThe standard enforces exact seasonal overrides for all Triodia services:\n\n### A. Great Lent (Triodion Weekdays & Sundays)\n* **Lenten Weekdays (Mon–Fri)**:\n  - *\"God is the Lord\"* replaced with *\"Alleluia\"* and the 3 Lenten Hymns to the Trinity in the Tone of the Week.\n  - Kathismata: 3 Kathismata at Matins + 1 Kathisma at Hours + 1 Kathisma at Vespers.\n  - Canons: 3-Ode Canons (Triodia) from the Triodion replace the Octoechos canons.\n  - Prayer of St. Ephrem: 4 Great Prostrations + 12 Metanias + 1 Great Prostration recited at all offices.\n  - Vespers: Presanctified Liturgy on Wednesdays and Fridays (10 Stichera: 6 Triodion + 4 Menaion; Old Testament Genesis & Proverbs).\n* **Lenten Sundays (Sundays 1–5)**:\n  - Sunday Resurrections + Triodion proper (e.g., Orthodoxy, Palamas, Cross, Climacus, Egypt).\n  - Liturgy: Liturgy of St. Basil the Great (10 Sundays: Lent 1–5, Palm Sunday eve, Holy Thursday, Holy Saturday, Nativity Eve, Theophany Eve).\n  - Evening Vespers: Great Prokeimenon (*\"Turn not away Thy face...\"* / *\"Thou hast given an inheritance...\"*) + 10 Stichera (4 Octoechos Penitential + 3 Triodion + 3 Menaion) + Lenten Dismissal Troparia with bows.\n\n### B. Holy Week (Lenten Climax)\n* **Great & Holy Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday**:\n  - Bridegroom Matins (*\"Behold, the Bridegroom comes at midnight...\"* + Exapostilarion *\"Thy Bridal Chamber...\"*).\n  - Liturgy of the Presanctified Gifts (Gospel readings of the Passion prophecies).\n* **Great & Holy Thursday**:\n  - Matins of the Mystical Supper; Vesperal Liturgy of St. Basil (Cherubic Hymn replaced by *\"Of Thy Mystical Supper...\"*).\n* **Great & Holy Friday**:\n  - Matins of the 12 Passion Gospels; Royal Hours (1st, 3rd, 6th, 9th); Vespers of the Deposition (Shroud / Plashchanytsia procession).\n* **Great & Holy Saturday**:\n  - Matins of the Lamentations (Psalm 118 with Enkomia around the Tomb).\n  - Vesperal Liturgy of St. Basil (15 Old Testament Readings; *\"Arise, O God\"* with clergy vesting in White).\n\n### C. Pentecostarion (Bright Week to All Saints)\n* **Bright Week (Pascha to Bright Saturday)**:\n  - Complete Paschal Ordo: Paschal Matins (Paschal Canon of St. John of Damascus, Paschal Stichera, Golden Homily of St. John Chrysostom).\n  - Paschal Hours (all psalms replaced by Paschal Troparia, *\"Having beheld the Resurrection\"*, Ypakoë, Kontakion).\n  - Royal Doors remain open 24/7.\n* **Paschal Sundays & Weekdays**:\n  - Troparion *\"Christ is risen\"* prefixed 3x to all services.\n  - Troparia sequence: Paschal Troparion ➔ Sunday Resurrection ➔ Feast/Saint.\n  - Ode 9: Replacement of Magnificat with the Paschal Refrains and Irmos (*\"The angel cried...\"* / *\"Shine, shine, O New Jerusalem...\"*).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Automated Universal Compliance Equation\n\nFor any given calendar date $D$, the engine's output across all 7 cards evaluates to `PASS` if and only if:\n\n$$\\text{Card}(D) \\equiv \\text{DolnytskyRule}(\\text{Paradigm}(D), \\text{Season}(D)) \\land \\text{ToneMatch}(\\text{Hymns}(D)) = \\text{True}$$\n\nEvery audited card must be validated by automated unit tests in `tests/test_canonical_audit_truth.py` asserting exact compliance against this unified standard.\n","Description":"Codify Universal Canonical Maximalist Typikon Digest Standard in artifact directory","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\augus\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md","toolAction":"Writing Universal Maximalist Digest Standard","toolSummary":"Writing canonical_maximalist_digest_standard.md"}}]}
